      "writtenOn": "2021-03-25T12:37:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my opinion we don\u0027t check it because max_request_mv is one value for all PD ports. Checking pd_get_max_voltage() !\u003d new_voltage_limit would cause problems in the following code\n```\n for (port \u003d 0; port \u003c CONFIG_USB_PD_PORT_MAX_COUNT; port++)\n        pd_set_external_voltage_limit(port, max_pd_voltage_mv);\n```\nespecially when active charge port is 1.",
      "parentUuid": "026778e7_693fbff6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 741,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 741,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "be32f493a3991d8ce3090e64bb9ab006d942623b",
